event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":108,"item_id":"rs_094103005b98f82f016aca927759ec81978e2c990a9cb46c58","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Evaluating implementation steps**\n\nI need to consider whether my time budget of 8k tokens is enough for what I'm trying to accomplish. I want to implement a server form for a checkbox endpoint that processes a POST request at /projects/id/tasks/id/completion with JSON. I'll use JavaScript to handle the onchange event for the checkbox, making sure to disable it while saving, and update filtering accordingly. It's crucial to retain task visibility and address any title creation errors effectively. I'll also try to reuse the existing body block in my helper for error handling."}

event: response.reasoning_summary_part.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_part.done","sequence_number":109,"item_id":"rs_094103005b98f82f016aca927759ec81978e2c990a9cb46c58","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"part":{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Evaluating implementation steps**\n\nI need to consider whether my time budget of 8k tokens is enough for what I'm trying to accomplish. I want to implement a server form for a checkbox endpoint that processes a POST request at /projects/id/tasks/id/completion with JSON. I'll use JavaScript to handle the onchange event for the checkbox, making sure to disable it while saving, and update filtering accordingly. It's crucial to retain task visibility and address any title creation errors effectively. I'll also try to reuse the existing body block in my helper for error handling."}}

